==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|gobbledegook}}; [[gobblygook]], [[garbley gook]], [[gobbly-gook]]

===Etymology===
First attested in a memo by US Representative (Texas) {{w|Maury Maverick}} dated March 30, 1944, banning "gobbledygook language". Apparently coined in imitation of the sounds made by a turkey.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-gobbledygook.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} [[nonsense|Nonsense]]; [[meaningless]] or [[encrypted]] language.
# {{lb|en|informal}} Something written in an overly [[complex]], [[incoherent]], or [[incomprehensible]] manner.

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Thesaurus:nonsense]]

